{"availability":"available","full":"abognar-git/poisoned-well","name":"poisoned-well","description":"A Russian propaganda network runs one site per target country - which makes its siblings a control group. Pointed at Hungary's 2026 election, the instrument took away four of my own published findings and left one number standing.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-12T11:19:15Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:13:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://abognar-git.github.io/poisoned-well/","topics":["data-journalism","disinformation","elections","hungary","influence-operations","information-operations","investigative-journalism","media-analysis","misinformation","open-source-intelligence","osint","propaganda","python","threat-intelligence","web-scraping"],"demo":"https://abognar-git.github.io/poisoned-well/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.449Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.449Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.449Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.449Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Russian propaganda network runs one website per target country. That means every claim you make about one of them can be checked against a hundred siblings — including the claims you would rather keep.","I built the instrument that does the checking and pointed it at the mirror aimed at Hungary's April 2026 election. It took away four of my own published findings and cut a fifth down to a fifteen-day gap it cannot explain. What survived is one number: across 149,490 articles and the 973 sources that account for all of them, the Hungarian pro-government press is credited zero times.","How to read this. The section below stands on its own — it is the whole project in about five minutes, in plain language. Everything after it is the evidence: how the instrument works, one finding followed from claim to retraction, then the results for someone who wants to check the numbers, then what went wrong and what this cannot show. Stopping after the first section is a perfectly good way to read it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abognar-git/poisoned-well/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"80a49ac0107e9e1fc7f3b4a5115ddab52c4707beb6700e3ca46bd72870deef4c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.541Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.541Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Russian propaganda network runs one website per target country. That means every claim you make about one of them can be checked against a hundred siblings — including the claims you would rather keep.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abognar-git/poisoned-well/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"80a49ac0107e9e1fc7f3b4a5115ddab52c4707beb6700e3ca46bd72870deef4c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abognar-git/poisoned-well/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.541Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T07:13:44Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abognar-git/poisoned-well/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.543Z","hash":"80a49ac0107e9e1fc7f3b4a5115ddab52c4707beb6700e3ca46bd72870deef4c","originalBytes":35718,"storedBytes":35718,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["what","one","mirror","every","data","scripts","own","same","figures","channels","claim","hungarian","rather","them","check","four","network","three","two","python3","window","against","does","only","published","they","finding","after","how","it.","day","never","panel","were","which","because","cannot","case","catalog","census","hungary","other","read","claims","did","each","election","file","had","here","project","runs","about","articles","chance","credits","found","number","registered","source","where","april","carries","derive","docs","domestic","five","mirrors","output","page","article","before","